  <h1>Interests</h1>
  <p class="intro">What I spend my time on, roughly in order of how much of it they take.</p>

  <p>
    I am fascinated by how everything works, and by the nature of the universe we find ourselves
    in. That curiosity lands most often on two things: artificial intelligence and human
    consciousness. Most of what I read and build sits somewhere between them: how these systems
    come to behave the way they do, and what that does or does not tell us about how we do.
  </p>

  <p>
    Beyond those, I follow history, philosophy, psychology, geopolitics, economics, and
    financial markets. Most of that learning happens on LinkedIn, X, and YouTube, and it is
    where a lot of my spare attention goes.
  </p>

  <p>
    I also enjoy teaching and public speaking. Explaining something to an audience is the
    fastest way I know to find the gaps in my own understanding, which is a large part of why I
    keep <a href="/notes/">notes</a> here at all.
  </p>

  <p>
    Away from a screen, I work out (mostly strength training), run, and play sports whenever I
    get the chance. The ones I play most are table tennis, badminton, and football, in that
    order, which also happens to be the order of how good I am at each.
  </p>

  <p>
    I only really enjoy one video game, and that is FIFA, now EA Sports FC.
  </p>
</Base>

